its forms: " think", " thinking", " thinks", " Think", and "think" completed inside
a word (as in "rethink"). The size of the negative value depends on the word before
"think": after a subject pronoun ("I think", "you think") it is mild; after words
that set up deliberation ("let me think", "need to think") it is strong.
German "denk-" (denken, denke) is treated the same way. Near-synonyms (talk, thought, thing) are weakly negative, and a run of repeated
dot-leader tokens "··" gives a small constant negative value. Everything else,
including the chat-template tags <think> and </think>, is about zero.
"""

READS = ()

PRONOUNS = {"i", "you", "we", "they", "he", "she"}
SETUP = {"me", "to", "us", "let", "need", "'s"}
WEAK = {"talk": -1.5, "talking": -2.3, "talks": -1.2, "thought": -1.1,
        "thing": -0.9, "things": -0.4}


